From 3138e9a5ab8b31082b542fad520dfd20da8e6dba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:43:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(apk): resolve advisories through apk provided names on
 the vendor distros

The vendor keys its JDK advisories on openjdk<major>[-lite|-crac|...]
while the apk origin of the installed package is liberica<major>[-lite|...];
the two are connected only through the package's provides list
(openjdk21-lite-jdk-no-deps). Record the provided names in the apk metadata
(capabilities such as so:/cmd:/pc: and version constraints dropped) and, for
distros that use this convention (VendorLinux, VendorHardened), search the
distro feed under the first provided name it knows when neither the package
name nor its origin is known: every provided name, then every provided name
with the sub-package suffix stripped (the package name minus the origin).
The alias is searched like an origin package and reported as an indirect
match of the installed package. Other distros are untouched.
---
